# Names only: every value is empty. The application does not read a .env file by itself;
# export the variables you need into the process environment (shell, service manager, secret store).
# Delete the lines you do not set: an exported empty value is not the same as an unset one.
# Each variable is read in src/; search for its name to see its meaning and default.
# Never commit .env or put real keys in this file.

